{"id": 3969368, "title": "CVE-2026-80231: native CA store conn reuse", "submitted": "2026-08-25", "source_url": "https://hackerone.com/reports/3969368", "excerpt": "## Summary\n\n`native_ca_store` is in `struct ssl_config_data` (line 73 of `vtls_config.h`), not `ssl_primary_config`. `match_ssl_primary_config()` does not compare it. On macOS, `Curl_ssl_easy_config_complete()` (line 258) auto-sets `native_ca_store = TRUE` when no custom CA is configured — without modifying `ssl_options`. When `CURL_CA_BUNDLE` is defined, the auto-fill gives both transfers the same `primary.CAfile`, making all primary config fields match while `native_ca_store` differs.\n\nTransfer A (explicit `CURLOPT_CAINFO` = `CURL_CA_BUNDLE` path): `custom_cafile=TRUE`, auto-setting prevented, `native_ca_store=FALSE` — OpenSSL-only verification.\n\nTransfer B (no `CURLOPT_CAINFO`): auto-fill sets same `CAfile`, `custom_cafile=FALSE`, auto `native_ca_store=TRUE` — intended SecTrust verification.\n\n`match_ssl_primary_config` sees matching `CAfile` + `ssl_options` → connection reused. B inherits A's connection without SecTrust ever running.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nmacOS baremetal (`poc-native-ca.c`), built with `-DUSE_APPLE_SECTRUST=ON -DCURL_CA_BUNDLE=<path> -DCURL_USE_OPENSSL=ON`:\n\n1. Transfer A: explicit `CURLOPT_CAINFO` = `CURL_CA_BUNDLE` path → OpenSSL verifies\n2. Transfer B: no `CAINFO` → auto-fill, auto `native_ca_store=TRUE` → should use SecTrust\n3. Observe: `\"Reusing existing https: connection\"` — SecTrust never runs\n\n## Root cause trace\n\n1. `Curl_ssl_easy_config_complete()` (line 258): `!custom_capath && !custom_cafile && !custom_cablob` → `native_ca_store = TRUE`. Does NOT modify `ssl_options`.\n2. `CURL_CA_BUNDLE` auto-fill (line 269): sets `STRING_SSL_CAFILE` → `primary.CAfile` = bundle path.\n3. Transfer A explicitly sets `CURLOPT_CAINFO` to the same path → `custom_cafile=TRUE`, auto-setting prevented, `native_ca_store=FALSE`. Same `primary.CAfile`, same `ssl_options=0`.\n4. `match_ssl_primary_config` matches all fields → connection reused. `native_ca_store` not compared.\n\n## Remediation\n\nMove `native_ca_store` into `ssl_primary_config` so `match_ssl_primary_config()` compares it. Or add an explicit check in `Curl_ssl_conn_config_match()`.\n\n## Impact\n\nA transfer expecting SecTrust verification silently inherits an OpenSSL-only verified connection (or vice versa). Certificates trusted by one policy but not the other pass without re-verification.", "excerpt_truncated": false, "final": "likely_valid", "final_label": "Confirmed by the code", "tone": "good", "explain": "The real code shows the flaw the report describes.", "confidence": 0.95, "judge_verdict": "likely_valid", "receipts_override": "", "policy_section": "", "grounding": {"verdict": "partially_grounded", "rev": "7be1e70cb6bc", "rev_source": "master on 2026-08-25", "counts": {"grounded": 11, "ungrounded_strong": 0, "ungrounded_medium": 1}, "problems": [{"check": "line", "status": "ungrounded", "severity": "medium", "claim": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.h:73", "evidence": "none of native_ca_store, ssl_primary_config, match_ssl_primary_config, Curl_ssl_easy_config_complete appear near line 73 at 7be1e70cb6bc; it reads: 'list errors */'"}]}, "summary": "A transfer expecting SecTrust verification silently inherits an OpenSSL-only verified connection due to mismatched native_ca_store handling during connection reuse on macOS.", "claims": [{"id": "C1", "kind": "flaw", "text": "native_ca_store is not part of ssl_primary_config, so match_ssl_primary_config does not compare it", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "In the release version (curl-8_21_0), match_ssl_primary_config compares many fields but native_ca_store is absent from both the struct and the comparison. Master (7be1e70cb6bc) fixed this via commit 7be1e70cb6 which moved native_ca_store into ssl_primary_config and added the comparison at line 144 of current master.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 144, "note": "match_ssl_primary_config in release curl-8_21_0 does not compare native_ca_store (lines 149-176)", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 144, "note": "ssl_primary_config struct in release lacks native_ca_store field", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C2", "kind": "location", "text": "native_ca_store is in struct ssl_config_data (line 73 of vtls_config.h)", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "In the release, native_ca_store is a member of ssl_config_data (sslc), not ssl_primary_config. The deterministic check for master line 73 is irrelevant; the report describes the release code.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 260, "note": "sslc is struct ssl_config_data*; line 270 sets sslc->native_ca_store = TRUE", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 259, "note": "struct ssl_config_data *sslc = &data->set.ssl;", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C3", "kind": "trigger", "text": "CURL_CA_BUNDLE is defined and no CURLOPT_CAINFO is set, causing auto-fill to set primary.CAfile and native_ca_store=TRUE", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "When CURL_CA_BUNDLE is defined and no custom CA file is set (custom_cafile=FALSE), the auto-fill sets primary.CAfile to the bundle path and also sets native_ca_store=TRUE (since custom_capath, custom_cafile, custom_cablob are all false). Transfer A explicitly sets CURLOPT_CAINFO making custom_cafile=TRUE, blocking the auto-set of native_ca_store (stays FALSE) but ending up with the same primary.CAfile.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 269, "note": "if(!sslc->custom_capath && !sslc->custom_cafile && !sslc->custom_cablob) sslc->native_ca_store = TRUE;", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 279, "note": "#ifdef CURL_CA_BUNDLE block sets STRING_SSL_CAFILE to CURL_CA_BUNDLE when !sslc->custom_cafile", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 287, "note": "sslc->primary.CAfile = ssl_easy_steal(data, STRING_SSL_CAFILE_PROXY);", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C4", "kind": "impact", "text": "Transfer B inherits Transfer A's connection without SecTrust verification running", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "Because match_ssl_primary_config in the release does not compare native_ca_store, two transfers with identical primary.CAfile and ssl_options but different native_ca_store (FALSE vs TRUE) will match, causing connection reuse. Transfer B inherits Transfer A's OpenSSL-verified connection without SecTrust running.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 144, "note": "match_ssl_primary_config lacks native_ca_store comparison", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c", "line": 171, "note": "Curl_ssl_conn_config_match calls match_ssl_primary_config", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C5", "kind": "reproduction", "text": "macOS baremetal build with -DUSE_APPLE_SECTRUST=ON -DCURL_CA_BUNDLE=<path> -DCURL_USE_OPENSSL=ON shows \"Reusing existing https: connection\" for Transfer B", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The code path matches the reproduction: with USE_APPLE_SECTRUST and CURL_CA_BUNDLE defined, Transfer A (explicit CAINFO) gets native_ca_store=FALSE, Transfer B (no CAINFO) gets native_ca_store=TRUE and same CAfile. match_ssl_primary_config in release sees them as equal, logs connection reuse. The exact log message is not in provided snippets but the logic is sound.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 269, "note": "Auto-set of native_ca_store=TRUE guarded by USE_APPLE_SECTRUST || CURL_CA_NATIVE", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c@curl-8_21_0", "line": 279, "note": "CURL_CA_BUNDLE auto-fill sets primary.CAfile", "valid": true}]}], "external_checks": [], "external_sources": [{"url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/answers/questions/4848319/word-2010-mail-merge-if-comparison-between-fields", "title": "Word 2010 Mail Merge IF Comparison Between Fields - Microsoft Q&A", "for": "match_ssl_primary_config() compares all fields of ssl_primary_config except native_ca_store"}, {"url": "https://web.mit.edu/6.013_book/www/chapter3/3.3.html", "title": "3.3 Conditions for Fields to be Quasistatic", "for": "match_ssl_primary_config() compares all fields of ssl_primary_config except native_ca_store"}, {"url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/answers/questions/1658988/sharepoint-fields-(site-columns)-title-vs-internal", "title": "sharepoint fields (site columns) title vs internalname vs static name - Microsoft Q&A", "for": "match_ssl_primary_config() compares all fields of ssl_primary_config except native_ca_store"}], "key_reasons": ["The release curl-8_21_0 lacks native_ca_store in ssl_primary_config and does not compare it in match_ssl_primary_config (lines 144-180 of vtls_config.c@curl-8_21_0).", "Curl_ssl_easy_config_complete in the release auto-sets native_ca_store=TRUE when no custom CA is configured (line 270) and auto-fills primary.CAfile from CURL_CA_BUNDLE (lines 279-284), creating the exact mismatch the report describes.", "Connection reuse via Curl_ssl_conn_config_match calls the flawed match_ssl_primary_config, so Transfer B silently inherits Transfer A's OpenSSL-verified connection instead of performing SecTrust verification.", "Master (7be1e70cb6bc) already fixed this via commit 7be1e70cb6 which moved native_ca_store into ssl_primary_config and added the comparison (current master line 144), but the flaw exists in the latest release."], "missing_info": [], "reply": "Thank you for the detailed report. The flaw exists in curl-8.21.0: native_ca_store is not part of ssl_primary_config, so match_ssl_primary_config does not compare it, causing connection reuse between transfers with different native CA store settings. Master already contains the fix (commit 7be1e70cb6). We will ensure the fix is in the next release. Could you confirm the reproduction works with curl-8.21.0?", "code": [{"name": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c@curl-8_21_0", "start": 144, "end": 180, "reason": "definition of match_ssl_primary_config as in release curl-8_21_0; differs from master; commits that changed it since: 7be1e70cb6 vtls: move 'native_ca_store' ssl_config_data => ssl_primary_config | 69ac867f98 TLS: drop support for TLS-SRP", "rows": [{"n": 144, "text": "static bool match_ssl_primary_config(struct Curl_easy *data,", "notes": ["C1: match_ssl_primary_config in release curl-8_21_0 does not compare native_ca_store (lines 149-176)", "C1: ssl_primary_config struct in release lacks native_ca_store field", "C4: match_ssl_primary_config lacks native_ca_store comparison"]}, {"n": 145, "text": "                                     struct ssl_primary_config *c1,", "notes": []}, {"n": 146, "text": "                                     struct ssl_primary_config *c2)", "notes": []}, {"n": 147, "text": "{", "notes": []}, {"n": 148, "text": "  (void)data;", "notes": []}, {"n": 149, "text": "  if((c1->version == c2->version) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 150, "text": "     (c1->version_max == c2->version_max) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 151, "text": "     (c1->ssl_options == c2->ssl_options) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 152, "text": "     (c1->verifypeer == c2->verifypeer) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 153, "text": "     (c1->verifyhost == c2->verifyhost) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 154, "text": "     (c1->verifystatus == c2->verifystatus) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 155, "text": "     blobcmp(c1->cert_blob, c2->cert_blob) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 156, "text": "     blobcmp(c1->ca_info_blob, c2->ca_info_blob) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 157, "text": "     blobcmp(c1->issuercert_blob, c2->issuercert_blob) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 158, "text": "     blobcmp(c1->key_blob, c2->key_blob) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 159, "text": "     Curl_safecmp(c1->CApath, c2->CApath) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 160, "text": "     Curl_safecmp(c1->CAfile, c2->CAfile) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 161, "text": "     Curl_safecmp(c1->issuercert, c2->issuercert) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 162, "text": "     Curl_safecmp(c1->clientcert, c2->clientcert) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 163, "text": "#ifdef USE_TLS_SRP", "notes": []}, {"n": 164, "text": "     !Curl_timestrcmp(c1->username, c2->username) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 165, "text": "     !Curl_timestrcmp(c1->password, c2->password) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 166, "text": "#endif", "notes": []}, {"n": 167, "text": "     curl_strequal(c1->cipher_list, c2->cipher_list) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 168, "text": "     curl_strequal(c1->cipher_list13, c2->cipher_list13) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 169, "text": "     curl_strequal(c1->curves, c2->curves) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 170, "text": "     curl_strequal(c1->signature_algorithms, c2->signature_algorithms) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 171, "text": "     Curl_safecmp(c1->CRLfile, c2->CRLfile) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 172, "text": "     Curl_safecmp(c1->pinned_key, c2->pinned_key) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 173, "text": "     curl_strequal(c1->cert_type, c2->cert_type) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 174, "text": "     Curl_safecmp(c1->key, c2->key) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 175, "text": "     curl_strequal(c1->key_type, c2->key_type) &&", "notes": []}, {"n": 176, "text": "     !Curl_timestrcmp(c1->key_passwd, c2->key_passwd))", "notes": []}, {"n": 177, "text": "    return TRUE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 178, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 179, "text": "  return FALSE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 180, "text": "}", "notes": []}], "cited": true}, {"name": "lib/vtls/vtls_config.c@curl-8_21_0", "start": 256, "end": 380, "reason": "definition of Curl_ssl_easy_config_complete as in release curl-8_21_0; differs from master; commits that changed it since: 7be1e70cb6 vtls: move 'native_ca_store' ssl_config_data => ssl_primary_config | c8df3defd9 lib: new easy option string storage | 69ac867f98 TLS: drop support for TLS-SRP", "rows": [{"n": 256, "text": "CURLcode Curl_ssl_easy_co